    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a4836cca1208c95",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "25c7dc680396bf36b3310a6642ea73aad125664cfa3ab3ab41eb2b6560f001af",
      "text": "Upon arrival, you will be transferred to the hotel.\n\nSão Luís is a charming, historic town situated by the ocean, not far from the Lençóis Maranhenses region.\n\nThe historic center of São Luís is akin to an open-air museum, with countless architectural details and elements, where cobblestone streets give way to narrow alleys. One of the finest examples of 17th-century French architecture is the Palace of the Lions, with its staircase leading to the palace, flanked by intricately carved lion statues. São Luís is renowned as the reggae capital of Brazil, with the Jamaican rhythm being more popular here than in any other Brazilian city. Among the attractions of modern São Luís are not only museums, but also the 17th-century church, local markets, regional cuisine, and numerous beautiful beaches. On the beaches, you can enjoy windsurfing, diving, fishing, or simply relax and unwind. Accommodation is provided at the Luzeiros Hotel.\n\nOptional tour:\n\nCity Tour 4h (USD44)\n\nDuring the tour, you’ll explore the historic center, recognized as a UNESCO World Heritage site, with its colorful colonial facades and Portuguese tiles.",
